Git and GitHub
Used AI mainly for guidance on the team's Git workflow: cloning the repository, creating and switching branches (feature/product-module), and resolving the confusion between local merges and Pull Requests.
Also used it to understand why pushes to develop were rejected due to branch protection rules, and to correctly interpret the git pull / merge conflict editor (Vim) prompts after the leader merged the Pull Request.

Design decisions
No design decisions for the Product module were asked directly to the AI.
The entire architecture — classes, attributes, and methods for Product, VideoGame, Console, ProductPersistence, and ProductService — was strictly dictated by the approved class diagram provided by the team.
AI was used only to transcribe these exact specifications into code, ensuring the strict visibility rules (private attributes) and the use of @Override annotations were respected.

Java implementation
AI explained the reasoning and structure needed for the Product module (class hierarchy and layering).
It helped me understand how to structure ProductService to correctly instantiate and use ProductPersistence to save and load lists.
It also helped me interpret the necessity of adding a getId() method — which was not explicitly in the diagram — to fulfill the logic required by the updateStock(productId, quantity) method in the Service layer.
I wrote and adapted the actual implementation based on the diagram, while AI only assisted with syntax and structural logic.
During implementation, I encountered a NotSerializableException and resolved it by adding implements Serializable and serialVersionUID to Product.

Data files and preloaded data
I created the data/ folder manually and added a sellers.csv file with 3 preloaded sellers, as required by the workshop.
The products.dat file is generated automatically by ProductPersistence when the program saves product data.

What I did NOT ask AI to do
Did not ask AI to answer the Product design questions — those decisions were already made by the team beforehand.

Did not ask AI to generate the Product or Sale diagrams from scratch — they were built from our own analysis. AI only helped with Java syntax and Git commands.

Did not ask AI to make direct pushes or merge the Pull Request; that action was correctly handled by the Technical Lead after review.
